WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.734
-That's a movie star
right there, bud.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:03.834
You look sharp.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:04.868
Thanks so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.200
I appreciate it.
-Appreciate you.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.067
Thank you for having me.
-Thanks for coming back.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.667
And, also, now we can say you're
officially a New Yorker.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:12.167
-Hey!
-That's what I'm t-- Right?

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:14.234
Is this real?
-Yeah, yeah, man.

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:19.767
I've been on the road for about
four years, since January 2017.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:20.934
-Working?
-Yeah.

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:22.901
Working, working,
which I'm fortunate to

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:23.934
you know, be in that position.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.400
But now I got a place.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.267
I can sit down, you know,

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:30.334
get into a little bit
of normalcy, go for walks.

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.767
-Yes! Good. Welcome.
Do you love the city?

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.834
-Yeah. The city's beautiful.
I'm glad to be here.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.033
You know, it's always good to be
here during Christmastime.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.534
You know,
I'm back seeing theater.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.901
I'm trying to shop.
I just learned about amazon.com.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:45.133
You know? I'm serious.
Serious, man.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.801
-You just learned about it?
-Yeah.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.400
Like, you know, I mean,
everybody's kind of been,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.200
you know, telling me about it,
but I'm a guy --

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.234
I really don't like change.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:52.400
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.901
So it took me a long time
to get around to it.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.334
But now it's just like,
you know,

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.767
that's my pastime
right now is just --

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.234
-Mind -- A whole world --

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:07.634
-Soaps, rugs, face serums,
you know, a brush.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.801
I got a scale.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.801
It's normal things, right?

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.968
-But that's -- You don't have to
go out and shop for it.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.400
-Like I'm used to.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.501
You know, like, I'm used to
going out, standing in a line,

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:18.801
and things like that.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.868
They said, "No, man,
you got to get on amazon.com."

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:22.267
And I'm like --

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.100
-This is interesting, 'cause
you're here to talk about --

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.300
You're not even here for Amazon.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.601
You're here to talk about
"The Matrix."

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:29.133
-Right, but, like, I need to
spread the gospel, right?

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.467
Amazon.com.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.601
It will change your life.

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:34.767
-Alright, thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.234
I want to say
congrats on starting

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.234
your production company.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.234
-Yeah, yeah.
-Tell me about that.

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:39.667
-Thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:42.200
So, it was just announced
a couple days ago,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.000
my production company,
House Eleven10.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.934
is in partnership with Netflix,
so I'll be able to,

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:49.434
you know, produce my own films
and really put my ideas

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.467
out into the world.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.167
So I'm very, very
excited about that.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.634
-House Eleven10.
-House Eleven10, yeah.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.801
-Congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:58.601
-Yeah, thank you very much.
Appreciate it.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.300
It's named after the house
that I grew up in

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.267
in Oakland, California, 1110,
in Oakland, California.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.601
-Oh, congrats.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:07.601
-So, now one of the hats,
apparently, that comes with it

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.167
is job man.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.367
You know,
everybody hittin' me up,

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.133
you know, thinking that I'm
giving out jobs now.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.267
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.467
-Yeah, now you got
a production company,

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:16.634
they're like, "Hey, hire me.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:17.634
I'm the perfect person for --"

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.133
-Yeah, like,
"I don't know what I do,

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.334
I don't know what you do,

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:23.501
but I know
you're giving out jobs."

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.801
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.234
-You're like,
"No, I don't have an idea.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.767
I'm not building something yet,
but when I do --"

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:28.901
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.834
-You got a lot of people
sending you résumés?

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.901
-Oh, résumés and bad scripts.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:35.467
-Yeah, exactly.
Bad scripts, yeah, yeah.

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:38.701
-I know that -- I was reading,
you know, before acting,

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.067
you studied architecture

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:42.000
and that you still draw
in your free time.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.834
-Yeah, a little bit, little bit.
-What do you draw?

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.033
-It depends.

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:46.868
You know, it depends on
what I'm working on.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.767
Sometimes, I draw my characters.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:51.133
I try to draw buildings
and things like that

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.367
every once in a while
just to keep that muscle going.

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:55.767
Last year, I had
a lot of fun getting on my

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.901
Instagram Live with
my fans and supporters

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.400
and doing portraits
and things like that.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.200
-Yeah, I saw this. Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.534
-So, I have a thing,
but could you --

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:06.000
If I gave you
a marker and a paper,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.367
could you draw a portrait of me?

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.434
-Oh, yeah,
no doubt, no doubt, no doubt.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.634
Let's do it.
-Yeah.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:11.234
-I'll tell you what.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.367
Yeah.

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:13.968
I'll tell you what,
if you got yours --

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.367
Yeah, okay.
Okay, yeah, there you go.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.467
You grab
a marker, pen, and paper,

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.767
and we'll do it like this.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:22.601
We'll do 15 seconds.
But this is the rules, right?

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.367
We've got to keep eye contact
the entire time.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:26.367
-Oh, no.
-Yeah.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.901
-I can't look here?
-No, no, no, no.

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:30.868
You can't -- Just let your eye
follow the pen --

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:33.901
I mean, just let your hand
follow your eye.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.667
Here we go.
♪♪

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.567
Okay, we got some drawing music.
Okay, here we go.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.934
-You ready, bud?
-Yeah, okay, here we go. Boom.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.734
Uh-huh.
-Uh-huh. Yeah.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.734
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:49.100
-You got the swoop?
-Yeah. You see that? Yeah.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.534
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:53.667
I don't even know where --
I don't know where I am on this

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:56.267
or where -- Like,
I don't even know where I'm at.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:57.634
-Oh, how we doin'?

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.334
-'Cause I went -- Now I went to
the top of your head.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:00.400
-Oh, right. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.767
-You're just letting your eye --

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.534
Just kind of let your eye
just kind of go with the music.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:04.567
There you go.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.567
[ Both scatting ]

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:12.634
-I think I'm close as I can get
to when I'm done.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:13.634
Okay, ready?

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.634
[ Both scatting ]

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:24.100
Alright, let me see.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.234
That's not bad.
-I'll tell you what.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:34.000
-Here's mine right here.
-There we go.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.868
I swear, you're much better
looking than that.

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.767
That actually
weirdly looks like me, though.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:44.968
I will take that one.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:46.834
-I'm laughing because you
weren't supposed to be

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:48.167
better than me at this.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.734
I was supposed to be --
-What are you talking about?

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:51.734
That doesn't look like you.

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.834
Who is that?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.834
I'm going to sign it, man.

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:57.234
I'm going to sign it just 'cause

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.734
I don't know what
you're going to do with it.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:00.267
-Now, are you going to put your
real signature on there or --

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:01.834
-No. I signed it
"Pete Davidson."

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:05.300
-Oh, of course.
-Now it's worth something.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.834
Can we talk about "Matrix?"

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:08.267
-Yeah, let's talk about
"The Matrix."

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:11.667
Man, "The Matrix" is
so, so, so damn cool, man.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.701
I'm excited to be
stepping back into this world.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.434
-You're Morpheus. Well, yes.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:16.667
-Yeah. Yeah.
I mean, I can say it.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:17.968
-Okay.
-I'm Morpheus.

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:19.968
-I don't want to -- Yeah,
I can't say how you're Morpheus.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.834
-No, because they get mad when
I do say that I am Morpheus.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.133
You know what I'm saying.
-Super-fans.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.701
-Super-fans.
Because everybody is so loyal.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:26.801
And it makes sense.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:29.033
I mean, I'm loyal to
Laurence Fishburne

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.334
and, you know, to his Morpheus.

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:31.434
Let's give a round of applause.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:32.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Laurence Fi--

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.767
-Laurence Fishburne as Morpheus.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.834
-But I want to take --
If you can allow me

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:39.467
the opportunity to say,
I'm not --

00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:41.567
I was not hired to replace
Laurence Fishburne.

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:42.667
-No. No, no.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.667
-No. I was not also hired to do

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:47.701
a "Laurence Fishburne as
Morpheus" impersonation.

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:50.701
-No, that is not --
When you see it, you'll get it.

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:52.934
-When the film comes out,
it will make sense.

00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:54.501
It will be cool.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.901
-And if not, I still got paid.

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:58.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.901
-No, no, no. No, no.
[ Applause ]

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:02.601
It is fantastic.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:04.601
I was gonna ask
you, when did you, like,

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:07.067
realize you're in
a "Matrix" movie?

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:08.434
Like, did you freak out
at one point?

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.467
Did Keanu just go like, "Whoa!"

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:12.868
Or did he say something,
and you're like --

00:06:12.868 --> 00:06:15.767
-It was at the table read.
The first table read.

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:16.934
We're in San Francisco.
We're all around the table.

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:18.234
And, you know,
we try to be professional

00:06:18.234 --> 00:06:20.200
and things like that,
'cause, you know, you're actors.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.467
You don't want to -- You know,
you're in "The Matrix."

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:22.801
-Yeah. You can't be a fan.

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:27.300
-And Keanu says -- He says,
"I still know kung fu."

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.667
And, you know, it was just like,
"Oh, my God!

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:31.467
I'm in 'The Matrix'!"

00:06:31.467 --> 00:06:33.033
-"I'm in 'The Matrix'!"
-"I'm in 'The Matrix'!"

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:34.267
-Oh, my gosh!
-You know what I'm saying?

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:35.267
But it's cool. It's exciting.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:37.234
-If you're a fan, it pays off.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:40.067
It has so many cool things
and cool story lines.

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:41.834
I don't even know how
they even wrote the script.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:42.901
-Yeah.
-It's brilliant.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:43.934
-They're brilliant.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.334
-Alright, I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:51.234
Here is Yahya Abdul-Mateen II in
"The Matrix Resurrections."

00:06:51.234 --> 00:06:52.501
Take a look.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.267
-Oh.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:59.434
No. No, no, no, no.

00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:02.334
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!
What do you mean no?

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.968
You wanted this. You did this.
This was your idea.

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:06.300
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.667
It was a test.

00:07:07.667 --> 00:07:09.267
An experiment.

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:11.868
-An experiment?

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:13.067
-Yeah.

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:15.334
-You put me in a tiny...

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.968
left me to bang my head till I
nearly lost my [bleep]

00:07:17.968 --> 00:07:20.868
searching for you
as an experiment?

00:07:20.868 --> 00:07:21.934
-The exit is breaking down.

00:07:21.934 --> 00:07:23.033
-He hasn't taken the pill.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.300
-What? There is no time.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.167
-I know. I know.
He's -- he's having a moment.

00:07:26.167 --> 00:07:28.133
-Does he know how hard it was
to hack that mirror?

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:32.334
-It's still open.

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.601
-This -- this...

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:36.801
can't be real.

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:39.467
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.467 --> 00:07:41.801
Yahya Abdul-Mateen II.

